C/Rust declaration chains (extern const char, static inline, extern crate)
get negative values. Boolean declarations after access modifiers get positive
values, as does LinkedIn. Separate rules recognize common package paths,
MIME types, HTML attributes, sharing widgets, and typographic separators.
Line/document starts and attached whitespace distinguish some token uses.

These are local pattern approximations, not a general code classifier.
A 100-character trailing buffer resets at document boundaries. Unrecognized
patterns return zero; neither a model nor an arbitrary token-ID table is used.
